From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:13:38 -0500
Subject: feat: find routes and other places by the words of another browser

A person from Arc types "air traffic" and Stedding answers with nothing, because
no label says it, and none should. A few words are now search terms and nothing
else, in one table, stedding::FindWordsTable, which Settings and the command bar
both read. "air traffic", "air traffic control", "traffic", "routes" and
"routing" find the routes card; "profile" and "profiles" find a Space's
Independent session; "favorites" finds Essentials per row; "little arc" finds
little windows; "auto archive" finds the archive; "url bar" finds the address.
"boost" finds nothing (settings T58; commandbar K39). The last four are from
the map on the site's page for people leaving Arc.

In Settings a row carries its words in search-hint, on the element that holds
its label or on its settings-toggle-button. search_settings.ts reads the hint
from either, and when only the hint holds the word it marks the row's text whole,
since the word itself is nowhere on the page. The Stedding page brings the first
mark into view, for the same reason.

In the bar each place is an action, and a place that has a row already, a
preference's, is found by the table's words alone, so its name lists no second
row. In Cmd-T's tabs mode a place shows too, labelled Settings, under the tabs
and the archive and above the suggestions, for five letters or more and at most
two places, so a person who types "air traffic" and not Tab finds it. The typed
row stays first and chosen. Choosing a place opens the card (settings T57).

Why: the features exist and people from Arc do not find them (BACKLOG S-422).

Removable when: never as behaviour. The words may go when nobody comes from Arc.
